/*
The genotype call parser needs a KNOWN column layout, so the outfmt is pinned here next to the
subworkflow rather than left to each pipeline's modules.config to remember. It matches the default
`columns` in GENOTYPE_CALL; change one and you must change the other, which is why they live as close
together as the module system allows.

A caller that genuinely needs a different layout overrides both: `ext.args` here and `columns` in
genotype_opts. genotype_call.py validates the field count and names, so a mismatch fails loudly at
the first hit line instead of silently mis-parsing columns.

-max_target_seqs is generous on purpose. The call needs a real runner-up from a DIFFERENT reference
to compute a margin against, and in a dense typing database the top hits are often near-identical
neighbours of the same lineage. Cutting this too low can leave no distinct runner-up and make every
call look confident.
*/

process {
    // makeblastdb has no default dbtype and exits non-zero without it. This subworkflow types
    // nucleotide sequences with blastn, so nucl is the only coherent value — pinning it here means a
    // caller cannot forget it and get a mandatory-argument error from deep inside a container.
    withName: 'BLAST_MAKEBLASTDB' {
        ext.args = '-dbtype nucl'
    }
    withName: 'BLAST_BLASTN' {
        ext.args = '-outfmt "6 qseqid sseqid pident length qstart qend qlen slen bitscore" -max_target_seqs 50'
    }
}
